=== Dataset Output Format Matrix ===
Generated by: npm test (src/runner.test.ts)
Purpose: Canonical audit of all possible display states for dataset run results.
         Review this file to check formatting consistency across all states.

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Section 1: Full-detail three-line phase contract
Datasets: acyclic-control and basic (first two tiers).
Each case shows: Hydration: / Consumer probes: / Full Run:
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[Case 1] Hydration fail — stack overflow (both comparers)
  Hydration:     ❌ FAIL [both comparers: Maximum call stack size exceeded]
  Consumer probes: not run (hydration failed)
  Full Run:      not run (hydration failed)

[Case 2] Hydration fail — shared-reference mismatch (clean classification)
  Hydration:     ❌ FAIL — shared references were duplicated
  Consumer probes: not run (hydration failed)
  Full Run:      not run (hydration failed)

[Case 3] Hydration fail — fallback: two distinct comparer errors
  Hydration:     ❌ FAIL [smartCompare: dep target mismatch] [flatCompare: length wrong]
  Consumer probes: not run (hydration failed)
  Full Run:      not run (hydration failed)

[Case 4] Comparer conflict — comparers disagree
  Hydration:     🚨 CONFLICT — comparers disagree
  Consumer probes: not run (comparers conflicted)
  Full Run:      🚨 CONFLICT

[Case 5] Full pass — hydration ✅, naive-json ✅, cycle-flat ✅
  Hydration:     ✅ PASS
  Consumer probes: ✅ naive-json  ✅ cycle-flat (output ✅)
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 2.5ms | RAM: 0.1 MB

[Case 6] Hydration pass + naive-json ❌ + cycle-flat ✅ (expected cyclic failure)
         naive-json failure is informational; cycle-flat is authoritative → Full Run PASS
  Hydration:     ✅ PASS
  Consumer probes: ❌ naive-json  ✅ cycle-flat (output ✅)
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 2.5ms | RAM: 0.1 MB

[Case 7] Hydration pass + naive-json ✅ + cycle-flat ❌ (authoritative probe failure)
         cycle-flat fails → Full Run FAIL (despite naive-json passing)
  Hydration:     ✅ PASS
  Consumer probes: ✅ naive-json  ❌ cycle-flat
  Full Run:      ❌ FAIL

[Case 8] Hydration pass + naive-json ❌ + cycle-flat ❌ (both probes fail)
  Hydration:     ✅ PASS
  Consumer probes: ❌ naive-json  ❌ cycle-flat
  Full Run:      ❌ FAIL

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Section 2: Later-tier compact format
Datasets: medium, stress, extreme (after the cyclic baseline).
Output is deferred and batch-formatted by buildLaterDatasetLines.
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[Case 9] All pass, no omissions — compact "experiment stable" summary
  4 algorithms continued to pass — experiment stable.

[Case 10] Stable passes with omissions — individual entries (Naive Recursion skipped)
  Known failure omitted: Naive Recursion
[Reference Tracking] Map Tracker
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 22ms | RAM: 9.1 MB
[Topological] Tarjan SCC Layering
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 18ms | RAM: 8.5 MB
[Schema-Driven] Two-Pass Wire
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 20ms | RAM: 8.9 MB

[Case 11] New failure — Map Tracker newly fails (hydration ❌ for first time)
  Known failure omitted: Naive Recursion
[Reference Tracking] Map Tracker
  Hydration:     ❌ FAIL [both comparers: Maximum call stack size exceeded]
  Consumer probes: not run (hydration failed)
[Topological] Tarjan SCC Layering
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 18ms | RAM: 8.5 MB
[Schema-Driven] Two-Pass Wire
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 20ms | RAM: 8.9 MB

[Case 12] Known prior failure — Map Tracker already failed at earlier tier (omitted)
  Known failures omitted: Naive Recursion, Map Tracker
[Topological] Tarjan SCC Layering
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 18ms | RAM: 8.5 MB
[Schema-Driven] Two-Pass Wire
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 20ms | RAM: 8.9 MB

[Case 13] Conflict on later tier — Map Tracker comparers disagree (always surfaced)
  Known failure omitted: Naive Recursion
[Reference Tracking] Map Tracker
  Hydration:     🚨 CONFLICT — comparers disagree
  Full Run:      🚨 CONFLICT
[Topological] Tarjan SCC Layering
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 18ms | RAM: 8.5 MB
[Schema-Driven] Two-Pass Wire
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 20ms | RAM: 8.9 MB

[Case 14] Hydration pass + cycle-flat ❌ (authoritative probe fail) — two-line phase format
         probesFailed=true triggers "Hydration: ✅ PASS" + probe detail (no Full Run metrics)
  Known failure omitted: Naive Recursion
[Reference Tracking] Map Tracker
  Hydration:     ✅ PASS
  Consumer probes: ❌ FAIL — ✅ naive-json  ❌ cycle-flat
[Topological] Tarjan SCC Layering
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 18ms | RAM: 8.5 MB
[Schema-Driven] Two-Pass Wire
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 20ms | RAM: 8.9 MB

[Case 15] Probe fingerprint changed from baseline but all probes pass — change warning
  Known failure omitted: Naive Recursion
[Reference Tracking] Map Tracker
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 22ms | RAM: 9.1 MB
  Consumer probes: ⚠️  changed from baseline — ✅ naive-json  ✅ cycle-flat (output ✅)
[Topological] Tarjan SCC Layering
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 18ms | RAM: 8.5 MB
[Schema-Driven] Two-Pass Wire
  Full Run:      ✅ PASS | Time: 20ms | RAM: 8.9 MB

─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Section 3: Hydration failure display styles (classifyHydrationFailTag)
Shows how different error types are formatted for the Hydration: line.
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[Style A] Stack overflow — both comparers same error (bracket-tag consolidated)
  ❌ FAIL [both comparers: Maximum call stack size exceeded]

[Style B] Stack overflow — only smartCompare (bracket-tag, single comparer)
  ❌ FAIL [smartCompare: Maximum call stack size exceeded]

[Style C] Shared-reference mismatch — clean developer-friendly phrase
  ❌ FAIL — shared references were duplicated

[Style D] Shared-reference mismatch — "is paired with more than one" trigger
  ❌ FAIL — shared references were duplicated

[Style E] Fallback — both comparers same unrecognised error (consolidated)
  ❌ FAIL [both comparers: unexpected id at index 3]

[Style F] Fallback — distinct errors from each comparer (both shown)
  ❌ FAIL [smartCompare: dep length mismatch at node comp_0] [flatCompare: wrong dep target at index 1]

